# pletivo conformance snapshot
# case:    content-formats
# project: tests/conformance/fixtures/content-formats
# covers:
#   - .mdx page route with frontmatter and a layout
#   - .md and .mdx entries in one collection, rendered through entry.render()
#   - YAML data collection with anchors, folded and literal scalars, flow style
#   - GFM tables and autolinks in markdown output
#
# Recorded from the "bun-build" adapter, but this file is not tied to it:
# any runtime claiming pletivo rendering parity must reproduce it exactly.
# Values in [brackets] are normalized — see tests/conformance/normalize.ts.
#
# Regenerate:  UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 bun test tests/conformance
# Just this case:  UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 CONFORMANCE_CASE=content-formats bun test tests/conformance

--- pletivo:conformance emitted ---
docs/guide/index.html
docs/intro/index.html
handbook/index.html
index.html
sitemap.xml

--- pletivo:conformance docs/guide/index.html ---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Guide</title></head><body><article><p>MDX body: markdown prose plus an expression — 3 — evaluated at build time.</p>
<p class="mdx-element">A JSX element written inline in MDX.</p>
<ol>
<li>ordered item</li>
<li>ordered item with <code>inline code</code></li>
</ol></article></body></html>

--- pletivo:conformance docs/intro/index.html ---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Introduction</title></head><body><article><p>Plain markdown with <strong>bold</strong>, <em>emphasis</em> and <code>code</code>.</p>
<p>A GFM table:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Format</th>
<th>Frontmatter</th>
<th>Body compiled by</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>.md</code></td>
<td>yes</td>
<td>remark/rehype</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>.mdx</code></td>
<td>yes</td>
<td>@mdx-js/mdx</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<ul class="contains-task-list">
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled> task list item, done</li>
<li class="task-list-item"><input type="checkbox" disabled> task list item, open</li>
</ul>
<p>An autolink: <a href="https://example.com/intro">https://example.com/intro</a> and <del>struck through</del> text.</p>
<div class="raw-html-passthrough">raw HTML in markdown</div></article></body></html>

